abstract: >-
  Version 2.1.1: 841 deterministic black-box optimization problems with
  continuous, ordered discrete and categorical variables, independent of any
  solver. 697 problems derive from 55 classical base instances in seven
  variable-type patterns (C, D, K, DK, CD, CK, CDK) and three scale
  strategies; 144 belong to the synthetic Family BK (nominal categories with
  a controlled continuous-categorical interaction). Every problem has a
  known global optimum with a stated justification; self-contained
  MATLAB/Octave wrappers and self-contained Python files (identical
  values), reference optima, versioned targets and a
  solver-independent evaluation protocol are included. The domains are
  chosen so that the centre of the box is never the optimum. Version 1.0.0
  (continuous and mixed-variable suites of the GLODS-SI and GLODS-SI-Mix
  studies) remains available under tag v1.0.0.
keywords:
  - derivative-free optimization
  - benchmarking
  - mixed-variable optimization
  - categorical variables
  - known global optimum
  - black-box optimization
